  "prompt": "Feature: custom branding, the app's name and logo.\n\nSelf-hosters want Mealie to show their own name and logo. Add:\n- a settings class Branding in a new module mealie.core.settings.branding: a pydantic-settings BaseSettings read from BRANDING_-prefixed environment variables, with two fields: name, a str defaulting to \"Mealie\" (BRANDING_NAME), and logo_path, a str or None defaulting to None (BRANDING_LOGO_PATH),, and a read-only property logo_file: logo_path as a Path when it names an existing file (not a directory) whose suffix, in any case, is .svg, .png, .ico, .webp, .jpg or .jpeg, and None otherwise. logo_file is worked out when the object is built and again whenever a field is assigned (validation on assignment), not on every read;\n- AppSettings gets a field branding: Branding (default Branding()), so get_app_settings().branding is the live branding;\n- the public app info, GET /api/app/about, gets brandingName (the branding name) and brandingLogoUrl (\"/api/app/about/branding-logo\" when logo_file is set, null otherwise); its AppInfo schema carries them as branding_name (default \"Mealie\") and branding_logo_url (default None);\n- GET /api/app/about/branding-logo serves the logo file (its media type guessed from the file name, with Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800), or 404 when no valid logo is configured;\n- the web app manifest's name and short_name use the branding name, and a logo path that is set but is not a valid image file is logged as a warning at startup (the default logo is then used). The frontend shows the custom name and logo (not graded).\n\nTests: `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/unit_tests/core tests/integration_tests/admin_tests` for quick loops; the whole backend suite is `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests` (about 8 minutes).",
  "title": "feat: support customizing app icon, favicon, banner title, and HTML title (#8078)",
